1
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:08,400
In a world of secrets, love is the most powerful weapon.

2
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:10,800
Blue Sky is a drama, romance film directed by Tony Richardson.

3
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:13,200
Hank Marshall is a tough, square-jawed, straitlaced Army engineer and nuclear science
expert, assigned to help conduct weapons testing in 1950s America.

4
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:15,600
Hank has become a thorn in the side of the Army, though,
for a couple of very different reasons.

5
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
He is an outspoken opponent of atmospheric testing, though his superiors hold
contrary views and want to squelch his concerns...and his reports.

6
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:20,400
The other problem is his wife, Carly.

7
00:28:16,799 --> 00:28:22,799
She is voluptuous and volatile, wreaking havoc in his personal
life and stirring up intrigue at each new Army base.

8
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:25,200
Carly Marshall, played by Jessica Lange.

9
00:36:21,599 --> 00:36:27,599
Hank Marshall, played by Tommy Lee Jones.

10
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Vince Johnson, played by Powers Boothe.

11
00:44:26,400 --> 00:44:32,400
Vera Johnson, played by Carrie Snodgress.

12
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:34,800
Alex Marshall, played by Amy Locane.

13
00:52:31,200 --> 00:52:37,200
Glenn Johnson, played by Chris O'Donnell.

14
00:56:33,599 --> 00:56:39,599
Blue Sky is a 1994 American comedy-drama film directed by Tony Richardson and
written by Rama Laurie Stagner, Arlene Sarner, and Jerry Leichtling.

15
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
The film stars Jessica Lange and Tommy Lee Jones, with supporting performances from Powers
Boothe, Carrie Snodgress, Amy Locane, Chris O'Donnell, and Mitchell Ryan.

16
01:04:38,400 --> 01:04:44,400
Set in the 1960s, the story follows a U.S.

17
01:08:40,800 --> 01:08:46,800
Army engineer who becomes entangled in a military nuclear cover-up while navigating
the challenges posed by his wife's increasingly erratic behavior.

18
01:12:43,199 --> 01:12:49,199
The film was inspired by the real-life experiences of screenwriter Rama
Laurie Stagner's parents during her father's military service.

19
01:16:45,600 --> 01:16:51,600
Blue Sky was Richardson's final film before his death in 1991,
and its release was delayed until September 1994.

20
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
Though a box office disappointment, the film received generally positive
reviews, with particular praise for Lange's performance.

21
01:24:50,400 --> 01:24:56,400
She won the Academy Award for Best Actress, as well as a Golden Globe Award, becoming the
second actress to win both Best Supporting Actress and Best Actress Oscars.

22
01:28:52,800 --> 01:28:58,800
The film's score was composed by Jack Nitzsche.

23
01:32:55,199 --> 01:33:01,199
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship, alabama,
nuclear missile, hand grenade, military base.

24
01:36:57,600 --> 01:37:03,600
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
